2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2485) 'a plain fsync probe, trace-event correlation and a RAM-disk cluster arm, run against the bare libfdb_c commit loop.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2485) 'What produces the commits from 100 ms to 730 ms seen in every benchmark arm so far?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2485) '`results-contention-matrix5.log` (commit 6be7ddb) ran a bare libfdb_c loop with no SQLite and no VFS (the SQLite-on-FoundationDB virtual file system), so the VFS is not the cause. Slow-commit clusters (events within 0.25 s of each other) numbered 24 across 12 cells: 14 touched more than one process and 10 touched one, correcting an earlier report that every cluster touched more than one process. A lone process stalled in 2 of 3 repeats, so sharing alone does not explain the stalls. Server CPU stayed near half a core, ratekeeper reported `limited_by=workload` throughout, and the scratch trace logs held one SlowTask event in total and no disk-stall events.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2485) 'A cause counts only if a control reproduces or suppresses the stall on demand; otherwise it stays undetermined, with what was ruled out, built from log files.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2485) 'Find what produces the 100 ms to 730 ms commits
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2485) '- Run a plain C loop of `write` plus `fcntl(F_FULLFSYNC)` on the same volume as the scratch cluster, recording the maximum latency, both alone and alongside a commit loop; if it stalls the same way, FoundationDB is cleared as the cause.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2485) '- Correlate the wall-clock start of every slow commit against fdbserver trace events and against production `fdbmonitor` log activity; sample `fs_usage` or `iostat` during the cells; run a RAM-disk cluster arm on the Mac and the desk arm from the sibling scheduling probe.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2485) '- Run the two controls: `SIGSTOP` a scratch `fdbserver` for 300 ms and confirm the detector reports a multi-process cluster; run with no load and confirm no stalls are reported.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2485) '- Keep the three candidates separate and untested until a control decides each: the scratch tlog's fsync sharing the Mac's SSD with the production cluster, macOS scheduling of client processes, and a cluster-wide pause. Do not cite the commit-proxy latency lines in `status json` per cell; they are cluster-wide windows, repeated across cells.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2485) '- RFD66606-2382, the skateboard's manifest, which names datasource-store's SQLite VFS over FoundationDB as the store these commits were measured against.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2485  1 LINE
 Text:Written

